    "# Messages in LangChain\n",
    "\n",
    "LangChain uses message objects to represent a conversation history passed to chat models.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Common Message Types\n",
    "\n",
    "- **SystemMessage**: Sets behavior and rules for the assistant.\n",
    "- **HumanMessage**: Represents user input.\n",
    "- **AIMessage**: Represents model responses.\n",
    "- **ToolMessage**: Carries tool output back into the conversation.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why Messages Matter\n",
    "\n",
    "Messages preserve context across turns so the model can reason over prior instructions, user questions, and tool results.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Minimal Example\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from langchain_core.messages import SystemMessage, HumanMessage\n",
    "\n",
    "messages = [\n",
    "    SystemMessage(content=\"You are a helpful coding assistant.\"),\n",
    "    HumanMessage(content=\"Explain what an API is in one sentence.\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "```"
